Today I learn a fundamentals concepts about DevOps. 
“What is DevOps?” It is a way of working that makes software delivery fast and reliable. It does this by removing roadblocks like manual work and
miscommunication between development and operations, using automation, collaboration and tools like CI/CD.
“Is DevOps a role or a culture?” Both. It started as a culture and practices, and in practice it became a job with its own tools.
“DevOps vs SRE?” They share goals. DevOps emphasizes fast, automated delivery, while SRE emphasizes reliability.
“What problem does automation solve?” Manual work is slow, error-prone, hard to trace and hard to reproduce.
